      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-335680",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}=4x(1-2x)-xy \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}=-3y+2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{\u2217}=[0.5,\\,0]^{T},$ we get\n\n| $J({x}^{\u2217})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{\u2217}$ is \n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}."
